## Session summary

**Build 0.11.403, srcversion `A57E80734521469C86653B2`, compiles clean. Still must NOT be boarded** — five of GPT's eight stop-ship items remain open.

Closed GPT items **1** and **6D** from the sess57 review, and found two real defects while doing it.

**Item 1 (durability).** Added `mxfs_blkdev_flush_durable(mp)` — always issues `blkdev_issue_flush`, returns the failure, advances the epoch only on success. `mxfs_blkdev_flush_epoch`'s skip-under-`fua_disable` rests on a coherency argument plus a per-modify cost argument; neither covers a once-per-mount barrier that must survive a *target* power loss. Wired at barrier step (a) (failure aborts the mount) and per-slice in step (c) (failure keeps the slot out of `replayed`, so it is never published). **The live foreign-replay path had the identical hole and is the more common one** — `mxfs_dlm_foreign_replay_work_fn` bracketed its replay with `peer_joined_flush`, which under the default `fua_disable=1` issues no device flush at all, then destroyed both pieces of evidence that would have made anyone redo the replay.

**Item 6D (publication gating) — neither purge function could report failure at all.**

- `mxfs_dlm_caw_purge_dead_nodes_ex` returned a success-shaped count while silently swallowing per-slot read failures, CAS write failures, and retry exhaustion. Now accounts `unread`/`wfail` and returns `-EIO`.
- `mxfs_disklock_purge_node` swallowed the **heartbeat-zero write failure** — which *is* the cluster-wide "slice replayed" broadcast — so the caller logged `P163-RECOVERY-COMPLETE` with the dead node's HB record still ACTIVE. It also counted unreadable lock-record sectors as clean. Now returns a negative errno when the purge can't be proven complete.

`mxfs_v5_dlm_recovery_complete` is now `int` and reordered: CAW purge → durable flush → broadcast → local bookkeeping, each gating the next. The flush placement is load-bearing: the reverse order survives a power loss as "node gone, grants still held, no pending marker" (an unrecoverable wedge), while this order fails as "node still looks alive", which the death detector simply redoes. `mount_cohort_complete` now reports a `published` mask and the barrier fails the mount when it differs from `replayed`. The live path re-arms via a new `MXFS_REAPF_FREPLAY` reap duty on a 30 s retry.

**Criteria: NO.** Not production ready — 11 open defects, 4 critical; defect #1's step-4a work still has GPT items 2/5, 6B, 3, 4, 6C and 6H outstanding, and no rig cycle has been spent on the barrier yet.

